        ":question/problem": "Let\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We notice that $A$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $2$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $4\\times 4:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}={BA}_{4\\times 4}\n$$"
